meta {
  name: 401
  seq: 2
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer invalid-token
  X-Authorization: Bearer invalid-token
}

docs {
  # 401 Unauthorized

  Every request in this folder deliberately sends a hardcoded, invalid bearer token (the header
  override above, replacing the collection-level `{{token}}` headers) so it should be rejected
  with `401 Unauthorized` before it ever reaches the controller — see `UserContextInterceptor`,
  which validates the `X-Authorization` header and short-circuits the request on failure. The
  request path/id used doesn't matter since auth is checked first.
}
